<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The shared insect gene: chitin plates under the skin and feelers that catch
		every trace of scent and mana. Stat work is light - the species' real numbers
		live on the race defs (Races_InsectMamono_BS.xml); this gene marks a mamono as
		insect-born and flavours her body.

             No armor here: every insect race tracker already grants its species'
             sharp armor as a stat stage, and gene + tracker armor STACKS. The
             gene's job is identity, colour, and the things every mamono shares:
             chitin skin, feelers, full toxin immunity, the pheromone effect in
             InsectPheromones.cs, and insect flesh.

             skinColorBase sets the BASE skin colour, the one under her real colour
             and the one that shows if she has none: a caste with no palette of her
             own (the four castes still to be built), or a woman carrying this gene
             without one of the caste xenotypes. Every caste's real colour is her
             own three, listed on her xenotype (a PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours
             extension) and defined next door in Genes_InsectSkin.xml.

             That class, `PMM_Insects.Gene_InsectChitin`, is also why the shared
             gene is the place the roll lives: it is the one gene every insect
             caste carries, so a caste's colour needs nothing added anywhere but
             her own three defs and her list, and a woman transformed into one
             rolls hers when her genes land. Uses vanilla Biotech fields, so it all
             renders through the normal skin pipeline with no custom art.

             Grief: this gene is also what makes a caste mourn like a drone, but
             the relation thoughts are NOT written into its `nullifyingGenes` -
             the game prints that list on this very tooltip, twenty-two lines of
             dead relatives. The nullification is a marker plus a postfix instead,
             and no line of it shows anywhere: Patches/InsectGrief.xml and
             Source/Insects/InsectGrief.cs.
     -->
     <GeneDef>
             <defName>PMM_Gene_Insect</defName>
             <label>insectoid</label>
             <description>This woman's flesh hides chitin beneath the skin, and a pair of fine feelers drinks in the air around her - every scent, every thread of mana. She was born of the hives.</description>
             <geneClass>PMM_Insects.Gene_InsectChitin</geneClass>
             <iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_Insect</iconPath>
             <!-- Explicit white, and it is not decoration. `GeneDef.IconColor` falls back to
                  `skinColorBase` below when no `iconColor` is set, and the icon is drawn with
                  that colour multiplied into it - so this gene's hand-drawn art came out as
                  olive-grey murk (the heart's pink 208,85,148 rendering as 97,39,51). White
                  opts out. The castes' colour genes are the other half of the same
                  mechanism and WANT the tint; a coloured icon needs this line instead
                  (user's fix, 2026-09-30). -->
             <iconColor>(255,255,255)</iconColor>
             <displayCategory>Miscellaneous</displayCategory>
             <displayOrderInCategory>1000</displayOrderInCategory>
             <!-- User ruling 2026-09-27: this gene COSTS 1 metabolic efficiency;
                  it paid 1 before. Every insect caste carries this gene, so this
                  one line moves the whole family: each mamono's metabolic
                  efficiency drops by 2 and she eats more. -->
             <biostatMet>-1</biostatMet>
             <!-- Full immunity to environmental toxins, ruled 2026-09-20. Both
                  fields live on GeneDef, not on ThingDef - checked in the 1.6
                  assembly, where immuneToToxGasExposure exists on GeneDef and on
                  ApparelProperties only - so a race def cannot carry them, and a
                  gene is the only home for this. Every insect mamono carries this
                  gene, so the ruling is one line here rather than one line per
                  caste, and it also covers a woman corrupted into a mamono later.
                  The races keep their own ToxicEnvironmentResistance 0.8: buildup
                  is severity x (1 - resistance), so 0.8 plus the 1 below is
                  already past the point where buildup stops. The effect list
                  carries no line for the toxins (removed 2026-09-27): the game
                  prints "Toxic environment resistance +100%" for the offset
                  below by itself, and the old sentence only said that again. -->
             <immuneToToxGasExposure>true</immuneToToxGasExposure>
             <statOffsets>
                     <ToxicEnvironmentResistance>1</ToxicEnvironmentResistance>
             </statOffsets>
             <!-- Shared chitin BASE tone: muted olive-grey (120, 118, 89), under
                  whichever colour her caste rolled. It is what shows for a caste
                  with no palette of her own, and for the instant before the roll
                  lands. -->
             <skinColorBase>(120, 118, 89)</skinColorBase>
             <randomBrightnessFactor>0</randomBrightnessFactor>
             <!-- Only the lines the game does not print for itself live here, and
                  nothing that just says what the description above already says.
                  Two lines were dropped on request for that reason (2026-09-27):
                  the toxins one (the stat offset prints its own) and the feelers
                  one (her description ends on the feelers). -->
             <!-- Insect flesh, ruled 2026-09-20. This is the same effect VRE puts
                  on VRE_InsectFlesh, without that gene's terrain speed factors:
                  customMeatThingDef keeps her butchered meat insect meat, and
                  defsTreatedAsHumanMeat makes that meat count as human meat to
                  HER, so eating insect meat - her own kind included - is
                  cannibalism to a mamono, and stays ordinary food to everyone
                  else. Both fields belong to VEF's GeneExtension, so VEF owns the
                  behaviour; Meat_Megaspider is the insect meat vanilla's own
                  recipes list, borrowed the same way the races borrow it with
                  useMeatFrom. -->
             <modExtensions>
                     <li Class="VEF.Genes.GeneExtension">
                             <customMeatThingDef>Meat_Megaspider</customMeatThingDef>
                             <defsTreatedAsHumanMeat>
                                     <li>Meat_Megaspider</li>
                             </defsTreatedAsHumanMeat>
                     </li>
                     <!-- Opt out of core's old-age cure (ruled 2026-09-27). An insect
                          mamono ages like the bug she is, so the ailments of age land on
                          her, and VRE_RapidLifeCycle - already on the devil bug and the
                          ant arachne, and promising exactly this in its own description
                          - finally bites. Core looks for the marker CLASS and never for
                          this gene, so the two mods stay decoupled, and the class's own
                          comment is the contract. Her fertility is a separate switch and
                          deliberately left alone: she keeps the Mamono 100% floor unless
                          a sterile gene says otherwise. -->
                     <li Class="ProjectMamono.AllowsAgeAilmentsExtension" />
             </modExtensions>
	</GeneDef>

</Defs>
